2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] Thanks for sharing this batch — it reads as a coherent snapshot of a terminal-graphics playground
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] (biblispec) with three parallel demos (maze, traffic, grid/centipede) sharing a common
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] `terminal.ts` core. A few observations:
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] • Overall structure*
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] - `terminal.ts` is the shared abstraction (raw stdin polling, cursor codes, sleep/run loop) used by
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] `traffic.ts`, `grid.ts`, and `centipede.ts`.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] - `maze.md` documents the cellular-automaton "traffic" rules (▤/▥ generator states, ▣▣▣ car shift)
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] that `traffic.ts` implements almost verbatim — nice to see the design notes and code match up.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] - `win32ffi.ts` has a real FFI implementation (GetAsyncKeyState/GetCursorPos/midi), while
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] `macosffi.ts` is currently just stub functions returning empty arrays/undefined — so `grid.ts` on
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] macOS has no real keyboard/mouse/midi input yet. Worth flagging in case that's not intentional for
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] this pass.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] - `relay.md` was shared empty — let me know if that was meant to carry content.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] • Possible bugs worth a look*
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 1. `maze.ts` — the `Edge` enum only defines corner/side/center members:
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5]    enum Edge { CornerTopLeft, Top, CornerTopRight, Left, Center, Right, CornerBotLeft, Bottom, CornerBotRight }
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5]    but `getOutline`/`getEdge` reference `Edge.Cross`, `Edge.TeeLeft`, `Edge.TeeRight`,
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] `Edge.TeeUp`, `Edge.TeeDown`, `Edge.LineHoriz`, `Edge.LineVert`, none of which exist on `Edge`.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] Both functions are currently unused (nothing calls `udlr`, which is the only caller of `getEdge`),
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] so it's dead code for now, but it won't compile cleanly if referenced. Also `getOutline` and
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] `getEdge` are identical — likely one is a leftover duplicate.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 2. `centipede.ts` — `ship` is a plain string (`"🤖"`), but `grid.drawShape(ship, shipx, shipy, 0)`
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] is called where every other usage passes a `string[]` (e.g.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] `grid.drawShape(["🍄🍄🍄🍄🍄🍄🍄🍄🍄🍄"], ...)`). If `CharGrid.drawShape` expects an array of
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] lines, passing a bare string will iterate characters instead of rows — probably want
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] `grid.drawShape([ship], shipx, shipy, 0)`.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 3. `centipede.ts` — in `scanInput()`, `up/down/left/right` are computed from the escape sequence
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] but never used, and `resetGame()` is empty. Looks like scaffolding still in progress rather than a
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] bug, just flagging in case it was meant to wire into `shipx`/`shipy` movement.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] • Minor/style notes*
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] - `maze.ts` computes `double` and `triple` (via `doubleLines`/`tripleLines`) but only `wide` is
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] used as `src` — harmless but dead work.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] - `boxIndex()` in `maze.ts` is a large literal-string lookup table; works, but could be pinned to
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] actual bitmask math instead of string comparisons for legibility, if you ever want to revisit it.
2026-07-05 12:52:44 [claude-sonnet-5] 
