2026-07-06 04:25:28 [grok-build-0.1] • 1. `writepng.cpp` has bugs*
2026-07-06 04:25:28 [grok-build-0.1] - The buffer conversion logic is confusing and likely incorrect.
2026-07-06 04:25:28 [grok-build-0.1] - It's writing `bgrBuffer` (which is being treated as BGRA) while `png_set_bgr` is enabled.
2026-07-06 04:25:28 [grok-build-0.1] - The alpha handling is hardcoded to 255 inside the row loop, which is inefficient.
2026-07-06 04:25:28 [grok-build-0.1] - The function signature suggests `bgrBuffer` is a scratch buffer, but the usage is fragile.
2026-07-06 04:25:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-06 04:25:28 [grok-build-0.1] • 2. Dead / commented code*
2026-07-06 04:25:28 [grok-build-0.1] - Heavy use of commented-out code (especially FreeType and macOS snapshot).
