2026-07-07 21:00:45 [grok-build-0.1] ...
2026-07-07 21:00:45 [grok-build-0.1] let label = game.labels[org] || "";
2026-07-07 21:00:45 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-07 21:00:45 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-07 21:00:45 [grok-build-0.1] `rom1.labels` is a plain object, but you're assigning it to a `Map`. Then you're accessing it with
2026-07-07 21:00:45 [grok-build-0.1] `[]` instead of `.get()`. This will always return `undefined`.
2026-07-07 21:00:45 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-07 21:00:45 [grok-build-0.1] You probably want either:
2026-07-07 21:00:45 [grok-build-0.1] - Keep it as a plain object (`Record<string, string>`), or
2026-07-07 21:00:45 [grok-build-0.1] - Properly convert it to a Map in `setLabels()`.
