2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] • Performance Problems*
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] `stepConwayLife` + `countNeighbors` is currently very slow because:
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - `countNeighbors` calls `getPixel` 8 times per cell.
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - `getPixel` does wrapping math every time.
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - `writePixels` is called per row with per-pixel bit manipulation.
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] For a cellular automata grid, this is one of the most expensive patterns.
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] • Recommendations:*
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - Add a fast neighbor counting method that works directly on the bit data (especially since you
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] already have `span`).
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - Consider double-buffering more explicitly (you already have `readLayer`/`writeLayer`, which is
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] good).
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - The current `stepConwayLife` allocates a new `pixels` array every row — this can be hoisted.
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] • Inconsistency in Wrapping*
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - `getPixel` does toroidal wrapping.
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - `setPixel`, `rect`, `drawMask`, etc. do not.
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] This is a common source of bugs. You should decide on a consistent policy (either all wrap, or none
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] do, or make it explicit).
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] • Minor Issues*
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - `writePixels` has a subtle bug: it reads `word=this.data[offset]` before the loop but
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] only updates `offset` inside the loop under certain conditions. This can cause data corruption at
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] word boundaries.
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - `rect()` always sets bits to 1 (no `state` parameter).
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - `cool()` and `heat()` are interesting, but `heat()` only works on set bits and walks the data
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] inefficiently.
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
