2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] This is cleaner, but a few notes:
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] - You're using `Uint32Array` for character codes. That's fine, but consider whether you actually
2026-07-08 20:30:53 [grok-build-0.1] need 32 bits or if `Uint16Array` would be sufficient.
