2026-07-09 18:29:36 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:29:36 [grok-build-0.1] Overall Impression
2026-07-09 18:29:36 [grok-build-0.1] This is a surprisingly functional hand-written 6502 interpreter. The fact that you're already
2026-07-09 18:29:36 [grok-build-0.1] getting readable disassembly output with labels and memory visualization while running Centipede
2026-07-09 18:29:36 [grok-build-0.1] code is impressive. The structure is still readable even with the giant switch.
2026-07-09 18:29:36 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:29:36 [grok-build-0.1] However, it's starting to show the classic problems of a large opcode switch: duplication,
2026-07-09 18:29:36 [grok-build-0.1] inconsistent flag handling, and some subtle bugs.
2026-07-09 18:29:36 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:29:36 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
