2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] • Code Review: `machine.ts`*
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] This is a solid start on a 6502 interpreter aimed at running Centipede. The opcode coverage is
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] already quite good for a hand-written emulator, and the debugging output is useful.
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] However, there are several bugs, inconsistencies, and structural issues that will cause problems
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] (some already likely are).
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] Critical Bugs
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] • 1. JSR stack push is broken*
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] let sp = this.registers[register.SP];
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] this.memory[0x0100 + sp] = (returnAddr >> 8) & 0xFF;
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] this.registers[register.SP]--;
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] this.memory[0x0100 + sp - 1] = returnAddr & 0xFF;  // BUG: writes to wrong address
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] this.registers[register.SP]--;
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] This will corrupt the stack. Fix:
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] let sp = this.registers[register.SP];
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] this.memory[0x0100 + sp] = (returnAddr >> 8) & 0xFF;
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] sp = (sp - 1) & 0xFF;
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] this.memory[0x0100 + sp] = returnAddr & 0xFF;
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] sp = (sp - 1) & 0xFF;
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] this.registers[register.SP] = sp;
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] • 2. Labels access is broken*
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] let label = game.labels[org] || "";
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] `labels` is a `Map`, not an object. This will almost always be empty.
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] Change to:
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] let label = this.labels.get(org) || "";
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] • 3. Duplicate opcode*
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] `case 0xE4:` appears twice (CPX Zero Page). The second one will never be reached.
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:39:28 [grok-build-0.1] • 4. Type declarations are invalid*
