2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] On the NMOS 6502 (what Centipede uses), `0x64` is an illegal/undocumented opcode.
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] Behaviour
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] - 2-byte instruction: `64 xx`
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] - It performs a read from the zero-page address `xx`
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] - Does nothing else (no register changes, no flags)
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] - Effectively a NOP with a memory read side-effect
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] On the 65C02 it would be `STZ zp`, but we are not on 65C02 here.
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] Fix
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] Add this case inside the big `switch` in `interpret6502()` (put it near the other zero-page
2026-07-09 18:48:05 [grok-build-0.1] instructions, e.g. after the `0x60` RTS or near the `0x65` ADC):
