2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] Thanks for sharing. This is a substantial TypeScript 6502 arcade-machine emulator/debugger, with:
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - ROM loading for Centipede and Asteroids.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - A partially implemented Digital Vector Generator for Asteroids.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Terminal-based memory/display inspection for Centipede.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Interactive single-step / continuous execution controls.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - IRQ/vblank handling and input-mapped memory reads.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - A growing opcode interpreter, including common indexed, indirect, stack, arithmetic, branch, and
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] bit operations.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Trace output with labels, register status, cycle count, and a compact braille memory display.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] A few things that stand out:
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `reset` declares four parameters (`address, irq, reset, vectors`), but the `R` key path calls it
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] with three. TypeScript should flag that, and it may leave `hasDVG` as `undefined`.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Several members are used without visible declarations on `Machine`, such as `cyclecount` and
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] `hasDVG`. This is fine only when strict property checking is not enabled.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Some instructions still write directly to `memory`, while others go through `writeAddress`. For
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] an emulator with memory-mapped hardware, routing all writes through `writeAddress` will
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] matter—particularly `STA ($nn),Y`, absolute `INC`/`DEC`, and absolute `LSR`.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `tick()` advances by a fixed four cycles per instruction. That is a sensible temporary execution
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] clock, but it will make vblank timing and timing-sensitive ROM behaviour approximate until
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] individual opcode cycle counts, plus branch/page-cross penalties, are represented.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - The DVG decoder is clearly exploratory, especially `LABS` and the vector semantics, but the
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] instruction loop, banking choice, and control-flow operations give it a useful foundation.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `VectorGenerator` would eventually benefit from stack bounds checks: DVG calls can underflow or
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] overflow its eight-entry stack when decoding goes wrong.
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] Overall, it is a nicely direct, inspectable emulator rather than an overly abstract one—the trace
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] tooling and ROM labels should make bringing up additional opcodes and diagnosing game behaviour
2026-07-11 13:51:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] much easier.
