2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] On an NMOS 6502, D changes the result and carry behavior for those operations. If either ROM uses
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] BCD arithmetic, results and C will be wrong.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `SBC` overflow logic is wrong in every implemented SBC addressing mode.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	This affects `SBC #imm`, zero page, zero page X, and absolute Y. The code calculates V using the
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] complemented operand used internally for addition. For subtraction, overflow must be determined
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] using the original operand being subtracted.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	This does not change C itself, but can cause `BVS` / `BVC` to branch incorrectly after `SBC`.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] - The actual `SBC` carry/no-borrow calculation is correct in binary mode.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	The implementation using `A + (operand ^ 0xFF) + C`, followed by setting C when the intermediate
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] result exceeds `0xFF`, is correct. The comment saying “result is >= 0” is misleading, but the
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] implementation is fine.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `setCarry` expects a boolean, but ASL passes a number.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	In the accumulator ASL implementation, `carry` is `0` or `1` and is passed directly to `setCarry`.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] JavaScript handles it correctly through truthiness, but TypeScript should object under normal
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] checking. This is a typing/clarity issue rather than an emulation bug.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Carry-sensitive instructions otherwise look correct:
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- `CLC` / `SEC`: correct.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- `CMP`, `CPX`, `CPY`: correctly set C when register ≥ operand.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- `LSR`: C receives old bit 0.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- `ASL`: C receives old bit 7.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- `ROL` and `ROR`: use old C as incoming bit and set C from the shifted-out bit.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- `BCC` / `BCS`: conditions are correct.
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] One adjacent status-register bug worth fixing: `RTI` currently masks with `~0x14`, which clears
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] both B and I. RTI must restore I from the status byte it pulled; clearing I unconditionally
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] can change interrupt behavior. It is not a carry bug, but it will make status restoration
2026-07-11 13:52:02 [gpt-5.6-terra] inaccurate.
