2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] Your existing binary ADC sequence is fundamentally correct:
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `carry = st & 1` produces `0` or `1`, suitable for arithmetic.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `result = a + value + carry` is the unadjusted binary sum.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `result > 0xff` correctly determines binary carry-out.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Your overflow expression is valid for binary addition:
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- overflow occurs when A and operand have the same sign, but the binary result has the opposite
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] sign.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- Your expression is algebraically equivalent to the more common `~(A ^ operand) & (A ^ result) &
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] $80` form.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Writing `result` into `Uint8Array` truncates it to eight bits. Explicit masking is clearer but
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] not necessary for binary behavior.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] For decimal ADC, preserve that binary sum before applying BCD corrections. It is needed for
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] the NMOS 6502’s status behavior:
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - V comes from the binary addition.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - On the original NMOS 6502 used in these Atari boards, N and Z also reflect the unadjusted
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] binary result, even though A receives the BCD-adjusted result.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - C must reflect whether the final decimal addition reaches 100 or above.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] BCD correction conceptually happens in two stages:
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 1. Add the lower decimal digits—low nibbles plus input carry.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	If that is greater than 9, add six to correct the invalid binary BCD digit.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 2. If the combined result is beyond decimal 99, add `$60`.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	The final overflow beyond eight bits is decimal carry.
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] So, for example:
2026-07-11 14:03:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
