2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] In `sbc(value)`, decimal handling belongs after calculating the unadjusted binary
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] subtraction and overflow, but before storing the result in A.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] Conceptually, the helper has these stages:
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 1. Read A, operand, C, and D.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 2. Perform the existing binary subtraction internally as:
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- `A + (~operand) + C`
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 3. Preserve that binary intermediate for:
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- overflow V;
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- NMOS decimal-mode N and Z;
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- no-borrow / carry determination.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 4. If D is set, adjust the intermediate result into packed BCD.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 5. Store the corrected low byte in A.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] For SBC, the incoming carry is inverted in meaning:
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `C = 1`: subtract without borrowing.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `C = 0`: subtract with an extra borrow of one.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] So the low-decimal-digit test must account for the incoming borrow. In terms of decimal digits:
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] low A digit - low operand digit - (1 - C)
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] If that value is negative, the low BCD digit borrowed from the high digit, so the binary
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] intermediate needs a decimal correction of `- $06`.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] Then, if the entire unadjusted subtraction borrowed—equivalently, the binary SBC intermediate has
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] no carry-out—you apply the high-digit correction of `- $60`.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] Examples, with D set:
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] ╭─────────┬───────────┬───────────┬──────────────────┬────────────╮
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  A      │  Operand  │  Input C  │  Decimal result  │  Output C  │
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] ├─────────┼───────────┼───────────┼──────────────────┼────────────┤
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] │ ---     │ ---:      │ ---:      │ ---:             │ ---:       │
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$42`  │  `$17`    │  1        │  `$25`           │  1         │
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$10`  │  `$01`    │  1        │  `$09`           │  1         │
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$00`  │  `$01`    │  1        │  `$99`           │  0         │
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$00`  │  `$00`    │  0        │  `$99`           │  0         │
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$50`  │  `$01`    │  0        │  `$48`           │  1         │
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] ╰─────────┴───────────┴───────────┴──────────────────┴────────────╯
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] The last case demonstrates the input borrow: `50 - 01 - 1 = $48`.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] For valid packed-BCD values, your existing binary carry test:
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] result > $ff
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] is also the correct no-borrow determination for decimal SBC. In the direct subtraction view, that
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] means:
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] A - value - (1 - C) >= 0
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] Unlike ADC, SBC’s decimal adjustments are subtraction corrections:
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] - low nibble borrowed: subtract `$06`;
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] - overall subtraction borrowed: subtract `$60`.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] And, as with your completed decimal ADC:
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] - V must use the binary result and original operand.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] - On an NMOS 6502, N and Z should use the unadjusted binary low byte.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] - A receives the BCD-corrected low byte.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] - C means no borrow.
2026-07-11 14:20:24 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
