2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] The new `sbc` decimal block currently applies ADC-style corrections, so it needs adjustment
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] before use.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] Problems in the current helper:
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - `nibble` uses addition. For SBC it must represent low-digit subtraction, including borrow:
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- low A digit minus low operand digit minus `(1 - carry)`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - A low-nibble borrow requires a subtract `06` correction, not `+ 06`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - An overall decimal borrow requires a subtract `60` correction, not `+ 60`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Carry/no-borrow should be derived from the original binary `diff`, not the BCD-adjusted `result`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - V must use `diff`, the binary intermediate—not `result`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - A currently receives `diff & ff`; it needs to receive the BCD-corrected `result & ff`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - NMOS N/Z should come from `diff & $ff`, which is consistent with how your `adc` helper uses
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] `sum`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] The intended flow is:
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 1. Calculate `diff = A + (~value) + C`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 2. Determine binary no-borrow from `diff > $ff`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 3. Calculate overflow from `A`, original `value`, and `diff`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 4. If decimal mode:
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- inspect `lowA - lowValue - (1 - C)`;
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- if negative, subtract `$06` from the result;
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	- if the binary subtraction borrowed (`diff <= ff`), subtract `60`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 5. Set C from the binary no-borrow condition.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 6. Store corrected `result` in A.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 7. Set N/Z from `diff & $ff`.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] For example, decimal `10 - 01` with C set:
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - binary `diff` low byte is `$0F`;
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - low nibble needs a borrow correction;
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - subtract `$06`;
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - A becomes `$09`;
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - C remains set.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] And decimal `00 - 01` with C set:
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - binary low byte is `$FF`;
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - low correction applies;
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - overall borrow applies, so subtract `$60`;
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - A becomes `$99`;
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] - C clears.
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] Your `adc` helper is still correct; this issue is limited to translating its correction structure
2026-07-11 14:25:39 [gpt-5.6-terra] directly into `sbc`.
