2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] loop run at import time. That makes `Machine` and `VectorGenerator` difficult to import into a test
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] harness without launching the emulator. Separating the CLI/bootstrap path from the reusable
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] emulator classes would help.
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Type mismatch in CRT helpers: `buildMemcode()` returns `string[][]`, while `dump()` is
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] declared to accept `Array<Array<number>>`. This should be caught by TypeScript under normal
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] checking.
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] - RTI status restoration appears incorrect: the RTI path masks with `~0x14`, which clears
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] both the Break and Interrupt Disable bits. A real RTI restores I from the stacked status; only
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] Break should generally be treated as non-persistent, while the unused bit remains set. This could
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] create interrupt timing errors.
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Memory-mapped access is inconsistent: some instruction implementations use
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] `readAddress()` / `writeAddress()`, while others access `this.memory[...]` directly. This means I/O
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] behaviour can vary by addressing mode. For example, indirect stores and several absolute
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] read-modify-write operations bypass `writeAddress()`.
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
