2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] zero, that becomes a negative typed-array index rather than wrapping to `$01FF`. The usual 8-bit
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] stack wrapping needs to be explicit.
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] - CPU timing is intentionally approximate: `tick()` always adds four cycles per
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] instruction. That is fine for bringing the machine up, but VBLANK timing, IRQ placement, and
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] software delay loops will diverge significantly until per-opcode cycle counts and branch/page-cross
2026-07-12 19:31:38 [gpt-5.6-terra] penalties are accounted for.
