2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] 🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.5 gpt-5.6-terra 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.202 183.4KB 24.00s
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] On an original Apple II, `C000–C0FF` is the I/O page. It is not ordinary RAM. Some
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] addresses are motherboard soft switches; others are delegated to expansion cards.
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] For a 1977/Apple II Plus-style machine, the useful map is:
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] ╭─────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  Address        │  Function                               │  Typical read behaviour                                                                         │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] ├─────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C000`        │  Keyboard data                          │  Returns key ASCII in bits 0–6; bit 7 is set when a key is waiting                              │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C010`        │  Clear keyboard strobe                  │  A read clears keyboard bit 7; return value is not usually important                            │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C020`        │  Cassette output toggle                 │  Read or write toggles cassette-output state                                                    │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C030`        │  Speaker toggle                         │  Read or write toggles speaker state                                                            │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C040–$C04F`  │  Cassette / utility soft-switch region  │  Exact use depends on machine/revision; usually not essential for a text-only initial emulator  │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C050`        │  Graphics mode                          │  Read or write selects graphics                                                                 │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C051`        │  Text mode                              │  Read or write selects text                                                                     │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C052`        │  Mixed graphics/text                    │  Read or write enables mixed mode                                                               │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C053`        │  Full graphics                          │  Read or write disables mixed mode                                                              │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C054`        │  Display page 1                         │  Read or write selects page 1                                                                   │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C055`        │  Display page 2                         │  Read or write selects page 2                                                                   │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C056`        │  Low-resolution graphics                │  Read or write selects lo-res graphics                                                          │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C057`        │  High-resolution graphics               │  Read or write selects hi-res graphics                                                          │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C058–$C05F`  │  Annunciator outputs                    │  Board/revision-dependent external-output switches                                              │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C060`        │  Cassette input                         │  Bit 7 represents cassette input level                                                          │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C061`        │  Pushbutton 0                           │  Bit 7 is set while button is pressed                                                           │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C062`        │  Pushbutton 1                           │  Bit 7 is set while button is pressed                                                           │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C063`        │  Pushbutton 2                           │  Bit 7 is set while button is pressed                                                           │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C064`        │  Paddle 0 timer                         │  Bit 7 remains set until paddle timer expires                                                   │
2026-07-15 11:26:07 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C065`        │  Paddle 1 timer                         │  Same                                                                                           │
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C066`        │  Paddle 2 timer                         │  Same                                                                                           │
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C067`        │  Paddle 3 timer                         │  Same                                                                                           │
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C070`        │  Paddle trigger                         │  Read or write starts/recharges paddle timers                                                   │
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C080–$C08F`  │  Language Card soft switches            │  Present only when a Language Card / compatible expansion is installed                          │
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] │  `$C090–$C0FF`  │  Expansion-slot I/O                     │  Slot-specific registers; 16 addresses per slot                                                 │
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] ╰─────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Keyboard: the first important missing device
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] For BASIC to become interactive, implement `C000` and `C010`.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] The Apple II keyboard protocol is:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] read $C000:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	bit 7 = 1 when a key is available
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	bits 0–6 = 7-bit key code
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] read $C010:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	clear bit 7 of the keyboard latch
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] For example, when `A` is typed:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C000 returns $C1    ; $80 ready flag | $41 ASCII "A"
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] After the monitor consumes it by touching `$C010`:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C000 returns $41    ; no pending-key flag
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] The monitor input routine normally waits with logic equivalent to:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] wait:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	LDA $C000
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	BPL wait	; wait until bit 7 is set
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	...
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	BIT $C010	; clear keyboard strobe
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Your current input handling is Atari-oriented:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] if(block==0xc00){
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	const byte=this.input[address&3];
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 	return byte;
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] }
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] That means `C000`, `C001`, `C002`, `C003`, and also `C010` currently come from the same four-byte
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] input array via `address & 3`. For Apple II support, `C000` and `$C010` need distinct handling
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] before that generic Atari block logic.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Speaker: `$C030`
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Every access toggles the speaker state:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] LDA $C030
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] or:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] STA $C030
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Both toggle it. There is no “speaker on” address and “speaker off” address. Software creates a tone
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] by touching `$C030` at a regular interval.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] For an initial emulator:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] - toggle a `speakerLevel` boolean;
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] - optionally record the cycle count of each transition;
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] - later translate transition timing into audio samples.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] The monitor boot trace has already entered `BELL`, and `BELL` eventually uses this mechanism.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Display switches: `C050–C057`
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] These are the switches already visible in the trace:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] LDA $C056	; select lo-res graphics mode
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] LDA $C054	; select text page 1
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] LDA $C051	; select text mode
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Representing the state separately is enough:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] textMode: true / false
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] mixedMode: true / false
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] page2: true / false
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] hiRes: true / false
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Although both reads and writes activate the switch, the monitor conventionally uses reads.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Game input: `C061–C070`
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Apple paddles are timed analogue inputs, rather than byte-valued registers.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] A program triggers all paddle timers:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] LDA $C070
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Then polls, for example, paddle 0:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] LDA $C064
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] BMI still_charging
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] - bit 7 stays high while the simulated timer is active;
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] - bit 7 becomes low after a duration corresponding to paddle position.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] A minimal implementation can return `$00` for all paddle reads, which represents a paddle timer
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] that has already expired. That avoids hangs in software that waits for it.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Pushbuttons are simpler:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C061: button 0 in bit 7
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C062: button 1 in bit 7
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C063: button 2 in bit 7
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Expansion slots: `C090–C0FF`
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] These ranges depend on the card installed in each physical slot:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C090–$C09F  slot 1 I/O
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C0A0–$C0AF  slot 2 I/O
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C0B0–$C0BF  slot 3 I/O
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C0C0–$C0CF  slot 4 I/O
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C0D0–$C0DF  slot 5 I/O
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C0E0–$C0EF  slot 6 I/O
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C0F0–$C0FF  slot 7 I/O
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] The conventional Disk II controller is usually in slot 6, so DOS-related software accesses
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] `C0E0–C0EF`. Those registers control drive selection, motor state, head phases, read mode, write
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] mode, and nibble data.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Slot ROMs appear immediately above the I/O page:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C100–$C1FF  slot 1 ROM
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] ...
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C600–$C6FF  slot 6 ROM, commonly Disk II boot ROM
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] ...
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] $C700–$C7FF  slot 7 ROM
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] The reset monitor can scan these ROMs to find bootable cards. So when you eventually emulate
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] booting from Disk II, you need both the slot-6 ROM at `C600–C6FF` and Disk II I/O behaviour at
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] `C0E0–C0EF`.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Language Card: `C080–C08F`
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] These switches belong to the optional 16 KiB Language Card, commonly present in Apple II Plus
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] systems running Applesoft BASIC.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] They control RAM/ROM banking and write-enable status for the `D000–FFFF` region. The access pattern
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] is deliberately odd: certain reads switch banks; paired accesses can enable writes.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] You do not need to implement this merely to run Integer BASIC and the monitor ROM shown in the
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] trace. It becomes necessary when:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] - the ROM configuration uses a Language Card,
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] - Applesoft is loaded into language-card RAM,
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] - DOS or a boot loader banks RAM over ROM.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] Practical implementation order
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] For the machine currently booting in the trace, the highest-value order is:
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 1. `C000` keyboard latch and `C010` strobe clear
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra]    Required to interact with the monitor/BASIC.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 2. `$C030` speaker toggle
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra]    Required for an authentic boot bell, though it can initially be silent.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 3. `C050–C057` display soft-switch state
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra]    Required to render the correct display mode/page.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 4. Text page memory rendering
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra]    Page 1 starts at `0400`; page 2 starts at `0800`.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra]    Apple II text rows are not linearly arranged in memory.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 5. `C061–C070` buttons and paddles
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra]    Needed for games.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 6. Slot 6 Disk II I/O (`C0E0–C0EF`)
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra]    Needed for disk booting and DOS.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] One architecture point: rather than testing only `address & 0xFF00 === 0x0C00`, dispatch the full
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] `C000–C0FF` address through an Apple-II-specific I/O handler. The same page is used very
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] differently by the Atari ROMs, so the active machine profile should decide which device bus owns
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] it.
2026-07-15 11:26:08 [gpt-5.6-terra] 
