2026-07-16 19:22:17 [deepseek-v4-flash] When you press the physical Backspace key (which your code maps to keycode `8`), the emulator
2026-07-16 19:22:17 [deepseek-v4-flash] pushes `08` into the key buffer. The monitor reads it, writes it to screen RAM (because it echoes
2026-07-16 19:22:17 [deepseek-v4-flash] all characters), and that’s the “odd character” you see—it’s the glyph for `08` in the Apple II
2026-07-16 19:22:17 [deepseek-v4-flash] character set.
2026-07-16 19:22:17 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-16 19:22:17 [deepseek-v4-flash] The Fix
2026-07-16 19:22:17 [deepseek-v4-flash] Change the backspace mapping in the main event loop to send Delete (`7F`) instead of `08`.
