2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] Certainly. Here are the 17 Integer BASIC commands grouped by their primary function:
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 1. Program Flow Control
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - END – Terminate program execution.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - FOR … NEXT – Create a counting loop.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - GOSUB … RETURN – Branch to a subroutine and return.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - GOTO – Unconditional jump to a line number.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - IF … THEN – Conditional execution.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - STOP – Halt execution (similar to END, but often used for debugging).
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 2. Input / Output
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - INPUT – Read a value from the keyboard.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - PRINT – Output text or values to the screen.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - LIST – Display the program listing.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - LOAD – Load a program from cassette tape.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - SAVE – Save a program to cassette tape.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 3. Variable Assignment
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - LET – Assign a value to a variable (the word `LET` was optional in Integer BASIC, but it
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] is a valid command).
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] 4. Program Management
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - NEW – Erase the current program and clear variables.
2026-07-24 16:45:59 [deepseek-v4-flash] - RUN – Start execution of the current program.
