2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] Thank you for sharing your ordering. I see you’ve grouped the commands by learning sequence, which
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] is a sensible approach. A few points to note:
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 1. PRINT appears twice – You listed it under “Input Output” as `PRINT, INPUT, PRINT`. It
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] should appear only once.
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 2. Missing commands – Your list does not include LET (variable assignment) or
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] REM (remarks/comments). Even though `LET` was optional in Integer BASIC, it is a valid
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] keyword and often taught early. `REM` is useful for documenting code.
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 3. Graphics – Integer BASIC (Apple I and early Apple II) had no graphics commands.
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] Graphics were added later in Applesoft BASIC (`HGR`, `HPLOT`, etc.). If you are creating a learning
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] outline for Integer BASIC, the graphics category would be empty.
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash]    If you intend this as a general “learning order for early BASIC” (including later dialects),
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] then graphics commands would belong in a separate group.
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 4. Immediate mode – The commands you listed are correct. However, `END` and `STOP` also
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] work in immediate mode (e.g., to halt a running program), but they are more commonly taught as
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] program‑flow commands.
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] Here is a corrected and complete version of your learning order (keeping your categories and adding
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] the two missing items):
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 17:00:03 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
