2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] program. That means Integer BASIC on the Apple II did have graphics commands, which I
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] mistakenly left out.
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] The Apple II version of Integer BASIC added the following low‑resolution (40×40 block) graphics
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] commands:
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] - GR – Enter low‑resolution graphics mode.
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] - TEXT – Return to text mode.
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] - COLOR – Set the drawing colour (0–15).
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] - PLOT – Plot a single block at (x, y).
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] - HLIN – Draw a horizontal line from x1 to x2 at row y.
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] - VLIN – Draw a vertical line from y1 to y2 at column x.
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] - SCRN – Read the colour of a block (function, not a command).
2026-07-24 17:01:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
