2026-07-24 20:08:09 [kimi-k3] • The middle ground I'd suggest:* ANSI 256-colour mode (`\x1b[38;5;Nm` / `\x1b[48;5;Nm`).
2026-07-24 20:08:09 [kimi-k3] It's not truecolour — it's a fixed 256-colour palette that every modern terminal supports,
2026-07-24 20:08:09 [kimi-k3] including the 6×6×6 colour cube plus a 24-step grey ramp. The escapes are short (~11 chars per
2026-07-24 20:08:09 [kimi-k3] attribute), and you can pick 16 palette indices that approximate the Apple II set far better:
2026-07-24 20:08:09 [kimi-k3] 
