2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] `C052/53` picks full vs mixed. Integer BASIC's `GR` touches both `C050` and `C053` (and `C056`, and
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] `C054` page 1). So a single `displayMode` enum works if you update it on every switch access, but
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] make sure `$C050` maps to "whatever the mixed/full state currently says" — tracking the two
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] underlying booleans (`textMode`, `mixedMode`) and deriving the enum is more faithful than setting
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] the enum directly.
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] 
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] 2. `$C053` is missing from your read switch — add it, or `GR`'s access falls through to the
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] halt case.
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] 
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] 3. Writes to `C0xx` still stop the machine (the `writeAddress` guard is unchanged from the
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] last review). This is the hard blocker: `GR` does `STA C050`, which currently logs and sets
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] `stepping=false`. The soft-switch cases need to be reachable from `writeAddress` too — on real
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] hardware, any access type triggers the switch.
2026-07-24 20:35:05 [kimi-k3] 
