2026-07-24 20:53:26 [kimi-k3] screen memory happened to be non-zero everywhere. On real hardware `GR` doesn't clear the screen —
2026-07-24 20:53:26 [kimi-k3] whatever was in the text page (usually leftover text bytes interpreted as colour pairs) becomes the
2026-07-24 20:53:26 [kimi-k3] graphics display, so a "noisy" pattern of colours is normal on first `GR`. A uniform field suggests
2026-07-24 20:53:26 [kimi-k3] either freshly-zeroed memory (but zero = black, not white...) or your `appleBlock` render of the
2026-07-24 20:53:26 [kimi-k3] boot-state bytes. If you `HOME` first, then `GR`, real hardware shows the space character (A0) as
2026-07-24 20:53:26 [kimi-k3] block pairs: A0 = high nibble 2 (dark blue), low nibble 0 (black) — dark blue over black stripes.
2026-07-24 20:53:26 [kimi-k3] Might be worth comparing.
